fbcon: add framebuffer console decorations (fbcondecor) with rotation
support, for the 4.9 (L4T) fbcon core

Backport of gavin_darkglider's 6.18 forward port (4200_fbcondecor-6.18.patch:
fbcondecor from jirka-grunt/fbcondecor 5.10, plus fbcon rotation support,
deferred I/O and the fixes listed there) to the 4.9 fbcon core in
drivers/video/console. The decoration code is the 6.18 code; what changed:

- 4.9 names: struct fbcon_ops (fbcon_par in 6.x), the console's fb from
  registered_fb[con2fb_map[]], vc_x/vc_y, asm/unaligned.h, kmod.h,
  fb_memcpy_tofb, a terminated sysctl table, no array3_size()
- in drivers/video/console next to fbcon, not part of fb.o: FB_CON_DECOR
  depends on FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y (fbcmap.c in the fb core calls in)
- 4.9 fbcon_clear() has no background color argument: the hook takes it
  the way the blitters do (get_color(vc_video_erase_char))
- 4.9 still has hardware scrollback (fbcon_scrolldelta, panning): off for
  decorated consoles, like scrolling (software scrollback redraws and is
  decorated)
- the helper workqueue is set up before fbcon_start(), whose takeover
  queues the decorations' setup when a framebuffer is already there
- the cursor buffer is sized for 4.9's largest fonts (32x32)
- Documentation/fb/fbcondecor.txt (4.9 has no .rst for fb)

